{{Quote|Come on, this is a little shortcut we use.|Jace Rucklin, upon showing Kazuda Xiono the lower deck entrance to the hangar|audio=LittleShortcut-FuelForTheFire.mp3|<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />}}
'''Jace Rucklin's hangar''' was located on the ''[[Colossus]]'' [[Trantor-class supertanker fuel depot|fueling station]]. In [[34 ABY]], [[Jace Rucklin]] and his [[Rucklin's team|team]] stored his [[Rucklin's racer|racing starfighter]] in the [[hangar]]'s upper deck. Along with his [[Racing starfighter|racer]], the crew had vehicle components and tools scattered about the upper area. In addition, the upper portion was outfitted with a large enough platform to hold a [[starfighter]] that could be lowered to give access to the lower deck. The lower deck, in turn, featured an opening that was sufficiently wide for a [[Starship|starfighter]] to exit the ''Colossus''. On the lower portion of the hangar, Rucklin also stored a pair of [[Speeder bike|speederbikes]].

==Description==
{{Quote|Whoa.|Kazuda Xiono, upon seeing Jace Rucklin's hangar|audio=Whoa-FuelForTheFire.mp3|<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />}}
[[File:JaceRucklinRacer-FuelForTheFire.jpg|thumb|left|300px|Jace Rucklin's hangar was large enough to store a starfighter.]]
Jace Rucklin's hangar<ref name="Topps">{{Topps|set=2019 Topps Star Wars Resistance|cardname=Kaz's Welcome Back|link=https://www.tcdb.com/viewcard.cfm/sid/202161/cid/12883928}}</ref> was located on the ''[[Colossus]]'' [[Trantor-class supertanker fuel depot|refueling station]] and featured an upper and lower deck. The [[hangar]] featured "A2" written in large [[Aurebesh]] letters on the wall of the upper deck as well as "B2" on the doors. The upper deck was able to house a [[racing starfighter]] and featured a platform that could lower a [[starfighter]] to the lower portion. Mechanical claws were situated on the lower deck to clamp onto the wings of a [[Starship|ship]] lowered from above and suspend it above the [[water]]s of<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" /> the [[planet]]<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars New Edition">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Castilon]]. The lower area was accessible via the ''Colossus''{{'s}} maintenance shafts. It featured enough room to store at least two [[Speeder bike|speederbikes]] and an opening large enough for a starship to exit the ''Colossus''.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />

==History==
{{Quote|Kaz, there you are. Did Yeager give you a hard time?|Jace Rucklin, to Kazuda Xiono in the hangar|audio=HardTime-FuelForTheFire.mp3|<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />}}
[[File:RucklinsLowerDeck-FuelForTheFire.png|thumb|right|300px|The lower deck of Jace Rucklin's hangar]]
In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="34 ABY">{{ResistanceDate|1|4}}</ref> the hangar was used by [[Jace Rucklin]] and his [[Rucklin's team|crew]], the [[Technician|mechanics]] [[Lin Gaava]] and [[Gorrak Wiles]], to store [[Rucklin's racer]] in the upper deck and his [[Rucklin's speederbike (blue)|blue]] and [[Rucklin's speederbike (orange)|orange]] [[speeder]]bikes in the lower deck. The hangar was filled with various vehicle components and tools and decorated with [[Painting|posters]], including ''[[Moves]]''. Soon after meeting the mechanic [[Kazuda Xiono]], who was avoiding his job, Rucklin showed him the entrance to the hangar's lower deck via a maintenance shaft. The two agreed to compete in a speederbike race out to a nearby [[sky ring]], but unbeknownst to Xiono, Wiles had rigged the bike that Xiono used to malfunction. After the race ended with Rucklin saving Xiono, the former's team left Xiono and returned to the hangar's upper deck to perform modifications on Rucklin's racer.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />

Wishing to escape the ire of his boss, [[Jarek Yeager]], Xiono visited the hangar's upper deck and expressed astonishment at the team's setup. After showing Xiono his racer, Rucklin convinced Xiono to sneak his team into [[Jarek Yeager's Repair Station|Yeager's private hangar]] with the ostensible purpose of seeing [[Jarek Yeager's racer|Yeager's ship]]&mdash;and the real intention of [[Thief|stealing]] a container of [[Coaxium|Corellian hyperfuel]] from the facility. The group waited for Yeager to take his break and then departed Rucklin's hangar to carry out Rucklin's ploy, with Wiles and Gaava acting as lookouts. Upon the success of the theft, Gaava, Rucklin, and Wiles returned to the hangar with their spoils. As the trio celebrated their victory, the hangar was revisited by Xiono, accompanied by the [[BB-series astromech droid|astromech droid]] [[BB-8]], who invited the team to a [[Diet|meal]] at [[Aunt Z's Tavern]]. The crew hid the [[Fuel|hyperfuel]] from Xiono as they turned the request down, citing an impending [[sky race]] as their excuse. Xiono subsequently wished the crew luck and departed the hangar with BB-8.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />

[[File:JacePreparesToRace-FuelForTheFire.png|thumb|left|300px|Jace Rucklin's team lowered his racer to the hangar's lower deck.]]
While Rucklin's team began adding the hyperfuel to his racer, Xiono became aware of Rucklin's thievery and the risk of explosion posed by using the hyperfuel. While Xiono raced to the hangar, Rucklin's racer was lowered from the upper deck to prepare for take-off. Gaava and Wiles watched from above as the racer ignited its [[engine]]s with metal clamps suspending it over the [[ocean]] below. Xiono employed the shortcut to the lower deck to arrive at the hangar before the race had begun and then leapt onto the racer and pleaded with Rucklin to stop. Ultimately, Xiono was forced to eject both Rucklin and himself from the [[cockpit]] before the ship exploded mid-race.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" />

==Behind the scenes==
The hangar first appeared in "[[Fuel for the Fire]],"<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" /> the fourth episode of the [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|first season]] of the ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'' animated television series which premiered on [[October 21]], [[2018]].<ref name="Disney Press">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref> Jace Rucklin's hangar was first previewed on [[October 17]] in the episode's trailer, which was posted on the official ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[Wikipedia:YouTube|YouTube]] channel.<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|qHX1x5ngIaI|Nice Bikes- "Fuel for the Fire" Preview &#124; Star Wars Resistance|date=2018-10-17}}</ref> In the episode guide that accompanied "Fuel for the Fire" and was posted on [[StarWars.com]], the hangar was identified as "Rucklin's hangar."<ref name="Episode Guide">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-resistance/fuel-for-the-fire-episode-gallery|text="Fuel For the Fire" Episode Gallery}} {{C|Slide 5}}</ref> The [[Topps]] set [[2019 Topps Star Wars Resistance|''2019 Topps Star Wars Resistance Surprise Packs'']],<ref name="Topps" /> released [[April 10]], [[2019]],<ref name="Topps Release">{{WebCite|url=https://www.beckett.com/news/2019-topps-star-wars-resistance-surprise-packs|text=2019 Topps Star Wars Resistance Surprise Packs Checklist, Details, Date|author=Ryan Cracknell|date=2019-04-06|archivedate=20220817140801}}</ref> featured a card that identified the hangar as "Jace Rucklin's hangar."<ref name="Topps" />

[[File:Rucklinsracer-FuelfortheFireComic.png|thumb|right|300px|The lower deck of Jace Rucklin's hangar as depicted in the adaptation "Fuel for the Fire"]]
[[Molly Denmark]],<ref name="Designing Star Wars Resistance">{{SW|url=news/designing-star-wars-resistance|text=Designing ''Star Wars'': ''Star Wars Resistance''|author=[[Kristin Baver]]|date=2019-03-11}}</ref> senior color key artist for "Fuel for the Fire,"<ref name="Fuel for the Fire" /> created lighting concept for the hangar's lower deck that was posted on StarWars.com on [[March 11]], 2019.<ref name="Designing Star Wars Resistance" /> In the [[Star Wars comic books|comic]] adaptation "[[Fuel for the Fire (comic story)|Fuel for the Fire]]"&mdash;which was written by [[Alec Worley]], illustrated by [[Cosmo White]], and published by [[Panini]] Verlag<ref name="Fuel for the Fire (comic)">{{ResistanceAnimationCite|4|Fuel for the Fire (comic story)}}</ref> on [[November 20]], 2019<ref name="Star Wars Resistance Animation 3">[[Star Wars Resistance Animation 3|''Star Wars Resistance Animation'' 3]]</ref>&mdash;the lower hangar features a catwalk that would run alongside a ship preparing for take-off.<ref name="Fuel for the Fire (comic)" /> This article assumes the depiction in the television episode to be canonical.

